Hivemind (`/Users/lchingen/hivemind`) builds a library of theses (dated questions with numeric ladders) from financial documents, grouped into research groups (one group = one ongoing matter, e.g. "Blackwell/Rubin rollout"). The owner, Alex, wants to try: embedding recall of candidate theses and group cards, then **Jev** as the reranker/judge to decide membership and identity. His words: "JEV 就是个 system-1 模型 … tn-hivemind repo 用过" (Jev is a system-1 model; the old repository used it).

