/Users/lchingen/tn-hivemind/docs/DECISIONS.md:44:| S229 | **A configured judge is never skipped silently, and the gate replays the factor window.** The acceptance window could not be replayed offline (10 cache misses): the live run had skipped the Jev tag check because `with_credentials.py --only OPENAI_API_KEY`, the standard launch, gave it no `TYPESAFE_API_KEY` (`jev_tagger` returned None with a log line), while the offline harness injects a stand-in key and served 270 cached Jev judgments and 98 adjudications, which changed 89 relationship records on the first day, every later knowledge position (`seq`, which the band-check request carries) and so the band checks and decides. Every stage2-accept ledger (7) holds 0 Jev judgments against a configuration that names `--tag-mode cascade`; the gate's goldens hold 876 and 474. Now `jev_tagger` under `jev` or `cascade` without the key refuses the run (`SystemExit`), a run without the judge names `--tag-mode extraction`, and the launch instruction names both keys. The gate gains `factor window guard`: `evals/golden-factor-window-v1` resumes the accepted window (`accept-v142e`, 2026-07-23 .. 08-14) from a frozen copy of its build ledger and ops sidecar, cut at the start (`guard_loop.window_plan`, `window.py --cut-only`), under `factor-v2-r14`, the twin pinning what the run applied (ladder v142, validator v4, tag mode extraction); 0 cache misses, 65 s, the run's audit PASS; its reference differs from the live log only by those two lines. The factor path's living days (prints, judgments, band checks, the weekly registry, refreshes) are now in every gate (LESSONS 44). | `cli/sources.py`, `evals/golden-guard/guard_loop.py`, `run_guards.sh`, `config/runs/factor-v2-r14.json`; tests OPS-11, OPS-4; IMPLEMENTATION_LOG 2026-10-13. |
/Users/lchingen/tn-hivemind/docs/DECISIONS.md:116:| S157 | **Provider lines answer a ladder metric only when the company's own figures qualify them (strict), and the binder waits for phase 2's metric descriptors; the catalog first keeps the company's witnesses (census mechanism 15).** Mechanism 15's registration, revised after Claude's brief wrongly excluded the catalog's own company table lines (LESSONS 38), measures 62 provider-dependent items in poc4c and poc4b: 28 matching, 11 mismatched (18%: Amazon's company FCF +$1.232B and −$7.604B against the provider's −$2.472B and −$11.625B, which moves three initial states to `investment_recovery`; Apple's diluted EPS $2.01/$1.65 and $2.02/$1.57; Meta's capex with finance-lease principal $72.22B, $19.8B, $31.08B against property purchases), 23 undecidable, 60 placements available; the reviewer reproduced them. Kept strict: an undecidable binding places nothing and records a data need (LIVING_DOSSIER_PRD §0.5), since a third of the decidable provider readings disagree with the company. Its two census-right losses (Apple's operating margin, Greater China growth) are not a parser miss: `catalog.collapse_duplicates` prefers a provider statement line and deletes agreeing company lines, keeping their names in `merged_from` but not their cells (159 company lines, 1,402 witnesses in the three company catalogs). The identity of a company line with a ladder metric is not yet a closed contract (a "Total revenue" row is not consolidated revenue by its label; an EPS row's basis comes from its statement), and phase 2's ladder contract makes key metrics request-bound descriptors with their definition, measure and unit, which subsumes it (lesson 42). Order: a catalog version that keeps each merged company line's entries as witnesses beside the unchanged canonical series (no request, line id or value changes), then phase 2's descriptors, then this binder against revision 2's registration with the reviewer's added controls (deduplicated values, consolidated against segment scope, reported against adjusted EPS, Apple's consolidated row under its inherited `Operating expenses` section). | `evals/metric-binding-v1` (revisions 1 and 2; branch slice/metric-binding); Claude's position and the contract review (`docs/design/review/m15-contract/`); `data/catalog.py` `collapse_duplicates` read. |
/Users/lchingen/tn-hivemind/docs/DECISIONS.md:284:| S99 | **Catalog v7 is adopted.** `core.units` decides once what makes a table cell a percentage: `rate_measure` (a label names a percentage: "%", percent, percentage, per cent, mix, growth rate, yoy, qoq, year-over-year … growth, once a scale phrase such as "(in millions, except percentages)" and "percentage-of-completion" are removed; a label that names basis points names no registered unit), `table_measure` (a caption that declares percentages in a parenthesis: "(as a percentage of revenue)", "(in percentages)") and `table_cell_percent` (the cell prints "%", its label names a percentage, or its caption declares percentages). The filing-table writer, the observation admission rule and the catalog audit use it; their three word lists are gone. The run audit keeps its own vocabulary on purpose, as an independent check. **Admission checks both ways:** a company-table value is a percent exactly when its own evidence (the cell's quote, its column group, section and row, the caption) makes it a percentage, so a cell that prints "%" is never stored as money and a percent needs evidence; a label that names basis points is refused in any unit. **A table of percentages has its own lines:** the table key adds "percent" when the caption declares percentages. **One line holds one unit and basis:** the catalog builder refuses an entry offered to a line of another unit or basis (a note). **A percent sign printed on its own line is inside the cell's span,** so the evidence shows it. `filing-text-tables-v3`, `catalog-normalizer-v7`; golden v4 (`evals/golden-current-v4`) replaces golden v3, which reproduces from the tag `pre-catalog-v7-2026-10-04`; `daily-v4-12`, `capture-v4-4`. A ledger observed under v6 is not rewritten. | The stored defect: Meta's income statement data "(as a percentage of revenue)" (10-Q and 10-K) took the line ids of the same data "(in millions)", because the table key stopped at " (". The cells that print "%" (revenue 100, net income 26–39) were offered to the dollar lines and filed as their revisions (4 lines, 44 entries in 10 filings), which the duplicate collapse then hid; the other cells were not read. The three word lists disagreed on no stored row's outcome, but each missed what another read (the writer read no "%", basis points, growth rate or yoy in a label, and did not remove scale phrases; the audit read "share of", which names dollars in "share of earnings of equity investees"). All 1,265 percent cells kept spans without their "%", so admission could not check a percent against its evidence. Catalog v7 rebuilds the v6 raw payloads ($0): of 2,584 lines, 1,729 are identical, 853 differ only by the parser version and 624 percent spans that now reach their "%", none changes value or unit, and Meta gains 32 lines and renames 2 (its percentage-of-revenue tables, and its tax rate reconciliation "(in percentages)" with six rows v6 did not read). No new line is offered to a model call: golden v4 replays golden v3 with 0 cache misses and only the observation counts change (11,651 → 11,833); the 38 projections of a v6 and a v7 replay under one code are identical once wall-clock fields are masked (control: 23 differ against the original golden ledger); the formation guard passes on the v7 catalog ledger. The full gate passes (2,719 tests on the real and a jumping future clock; data, formation, loop and projection guards; run audit). Data guard on seven companies: 25,538 observations, 0 refused; controls: v4, v5 and v6 refused (v6: 276 percents its kept evidence does not show). The daily preflight under `daily-v4-12` verifies the golden v4 ledger (21,402 records, 0 refused). Two independent reviews (Codex gpt-6.1-sol): the first found admission checked a percent one way only (165 mutations of a cell that prints "%" into dollars were accepted), the second that the audit's ledger mode did not read the cell evidence; both are fixed, and the second judged the result mergeable. 17 of 17 mutants (evals/catalog-v7-build/mutation_check.py); N1's 22 of 22 still caught. |
