     1	# Operations: setup, commands, the daily run and recovery
     2	
     3	How to run the system. Start with [SYSTEM_DESIGN](ARCHITECTURE.md), including its
     4	[key log examples](ARCHITECTURE.md). What the stages do is in [ARCHITECTURE](ARCHITECTURE.md); the rules
     5	every run follows are in [AGENTS](../AGENTS.md). The operations notes as they stood before 2026-09-28, including the Codex-era pipeline, are in
     6	history/OPERATIONS_2026-09-28.md.
     7	
     8	## Setup
     9	
    10	- Python 3.10 or later and the standard library, plus `numpy` for the develop stage's nearest-neighbour search
    11	  (`requirements-develop.txt`). `pypdf` (`requirements-corpus.txt`) is the optional PDF adapter of source intake.
    12	- Run commands from the repository root (the scripts put `src` on the path; the unit suite needs `PYTHONPATH=src`). A
    13	  git worktree needs a `.runtime` symlink to the main checkout's `.runtime`.
    14	- **Credentials** are in `~/.config/tn-hivemind/credentials.json` (directory mode `0700`, file mode `0600`; plaintext
    15	  JSON protected by file permissions). Another owner-only file can be named with `TN_HIVEMIND_CREDENTIALS_FILE`.
    16	
    17	  | Variable | Used for |
    18	  | --- | --- |
    19	  | `OPENAI_API_KEY` | every model call (`gpt-6-luna`) and the embeddings |
    20	  | `TRUENORTH_MCP_TOKEN` | the TrueNorth MCP: sources, catalog, prices, consensus, calendars, holders |
    21	  | `TYPESAFE_API_KEY` | Jev, the relationship-tag judge: required by every configuration whose `--tag-mode` is `jev` or `cascade` (the current ones); without it the relations stage refuses the run (S229) |
    22	  | `DEEPSEEK_API_KEY` | historical records only |
    23	
    24	  `python3 scripts/with_credentials.py --check` reports which names are configured, without values and without a
    25	  network call. A command that needs a credential runs as
    26	  `python3 scripts/with_credentials.py --only VARIABLE[,…] -- COMMAND …`: the launcher injects only the selected fields
    27	  into that process, rejects group- or world-readable files, symlinks and unknown fields, and never prints a value.
    28	  Never read the file with `cat`, `env` or shell tracing, and never put a value in a command argument, a stored URL, a
    29	  log, a prompt or a database row. `models.truenorth` builds the token-bearing MCP URL in memory only, refuses redirects and
    30	  reports sanitized errors.
    31	- **Local stores:** locations and ownership are specified in
    32	  [ARCHITECTURE §4](ARCHITECTURE.md#4-records-and-stores). Run-specific ledgers and protected data are listed in
    33	  [CURRENT_STATE](CURRENT_STATE.md#open-defects); inspect any database path before writing.
