     1	"""Research groups (D149, D165, D166): a group is one ongoing matter with a name, a scope and aliases, the names the
     2	matter goes by (products, projects, parties). Identity and membership are decided by code from those names, the way an
     3	object's aliases and a scope's aliases already are; the model only declares a matter that no stored group is, and may
     4	cite groups. A declaration whose aliases hit a stored group is that group; a thesis whose own text (focus, question,
     5	scope) carries a group's alias joins it, when the thesis itself tracks a matter; a company's own financial line joins only
     6	by the model's citation. Company names and tickers are never aliases: a company is not a group."""
