    72	
    73	**An out-of-list target is not automatically a recall miss.**
    74	
    75	| Ledger | Raw merge/succession decisions | Target absent from that candidate’s own list | Raw repeat/replace decisions with nonempty targets | Evidence target absent from that pair’s own list |
    76	|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|
    77	| G | 14 | 2 | 154 | 4 |
    78	| E | 17 | 3 | 192 | 9 |
    79	| C | 21 | 1 | 115 | 0 |
    80	| S | 34 | 4 | 280 | 3 |
    81	
    82	These counts retain retries. Two C repeat decisions and one S repeat decision had empty targets and are excluded from the nonempty-target columns.
    83	
    84	All **10 candidate-list exceptions** need classification before scoring:
    85	
    86	- Four target another candidate, such as `c1`, rather than an existing thesis.
    87	- Four attempt a wrong-quantity or wrong-object merge: standalone CPU into total revenue, North America revenue into total revenue, or Amazon capex into an industry aggregate.
    88	- Two are extraneous candidate decisions in S record 40; that input’s stored handover contains no candidates.
    89	
    90	Thus this particular census finds **zero demonstrated correct candidate destinations lost from the own-list search**. It does not prove complete recall: a model can choose “new” precisely because the right thesis was never shown.
    91	
    92	The evidence-list exceptions include real ranking misses:
    93	
    94	- E records **83/84**, July 27: Huang’s qualification of the financing story chooses E.e122 or E.e123, shown elsewhere in the request but outside its own pair’s top 10. Record 85 reuses record 83’s request.
    95	- G record **90** chooses the earlier Ohio guarantee report G.e148.
    96	- G record **128** chooses the earlier agentic-AI statement G.e81.
    97	- E record **203** chooses Musk’s earlier stored exclusivity statement E.e479.
    98	
    99	Other exceptions name evidence not linked to the destination, malformed incoming IDs, or an unrelated old record. They must not be labelled retrieval successes.
   100	
   101	E records 83 and 84 have archive cost estimates of **$0.038485 and $0.039924**. Record 85 is not another independent paid sample. This illustrates both the cost of the failure and the need to deduplicate costs by archived request identity.
   102	
   103	The [build log, row 8](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-10-25-english/build-log.md) documents the earlier rule correction allowing a target shown elsewhere in the request when it belongs to the destination thesis. That historical correction is not a new finding of this review.
   104	
   105	**The revenue concentration is real; its entire count is not a semantic error count.**
   106	
   107	At E’s July 31 cutoff, sequence 259:
   108	
   109	- E.v2, NVIDIA Data Center revenue: **185 evidence items**.
   110	- E.v1, NVIDIA total revenue: **148**.
   111	- Their intersection: **99**.
   112	- Their union: **234 of 411 evidence items**, or **56.9%**.
   113	- Across the whole snapshot, **140/411** evidence items link to multiple theses.
   114	
   115	The current field-level multi-link count differs from the build log’s historical 133/411. I report the fresh count with its explicit cutoff rather than treating the two measurements as interchangeable.
   116	
   117	In G, **138/365**, or **37.8%**, link to multiple theses. Grouping has therefore not by itself removed evidence fan-out.
   118	
   119	A concrete case is E.e122/e123, the $250bn guarantee and separate $350bn chip-financing reports. Both eventually link to the two NVIDIA revenue theses. Neither English snapshot contains a `financing_amount` thesis. On the initiating Reuters input, G retains only the aggregate-spending statement; E also retains the two financing statements under revenue.
   120	
   121	This separates three problems:
   122	
   123	1. Missing a material question.
   124	2. Choosing where its evidence belongs.
   125	3. Finding earlier evidence after that destination is chosen.
   126	
   127	Retrieval directly addresses the third. A reranker cannot repair the first without taking over extraction’s responsibility. Nor should all indirect revenue evidence be declared wrong: the PRD explicitly conditions direct evidence handling on the available dependency structure.
   128	
