The evidence supports a small trial, but not a promised accuracy level. Jev’s old test mistakes were concentrated in treating background information as stronger evidence—the same kind of mistake that could merge related theses.

The gold also needs two clarifications before scoring: one “same” set is provisional, and two “different” pairs are explicitly whole-versus-part pairs. I’ll keep those limits visible in the estimates and experiment design.
