    16	`poc/eval/gold/grouping-identity-gold-2026-10-25.json`, digest in `SHA256SUMS`. Labelled as an analyst from the stored questions and their initiating evidence: 3 `same` sets (one provisional), 11 `related_not_same` pairs (the hard negatives: GAAP vs non-GAAP, level vs growth, 2026 vs 2027, population differences, part-of), 4 `different` pairs, and four matters with required and forbidden members across the English and Chinese ledgers (Rubin rollout; the hyperscaler capex cycle including each company's capex; the OpenAI–NVIDIA financing, scorable only on the Chinese ledger; China chip export controls), plus the separate company matters and four uncertain cases. The analyst's call that departs from the stored data: the capex cycle group should hold every hyperscaler's own capex thesis, so the grouped week's Amazon-in / Meta-out inconsistency (F7) is scored as two misses, not one error.
