    51	| hosted rerankers (Cohere Rerank) | the pricing page shows dedicated-instance prices ($4.00/hour or $2,500/month for a Medium instance) and defines a search unit as one query with up to 100 documents, with no per-search price listed ([pricing](https://cohere.com/pricing)) | not for a $0.05 POC |
    52	| LLM listwise reranking (RankGPT) | properly instructed LLMs rank passages competitively with, and sometimes better than, supervised cross-encoders such as monoT5 on TREC and BEIR; a distilled 440M model beat a 3B supervised model on BEIR ([Sun et al., EMNLP 2023](https://arxiv.org/abs/2304.09542)) | this is what the matching call already is, with more structure; at the published gpt-6-luna rates a listwise decision of ~1,500 input / 200 output tokens costs about $0.00025, so cost is not the reason to leave it |
    53	
    54	What the literature does not give us: a cross-encoder trained on passage relevance outputs *relevance*, not *identity*. "Hyperscaler capex 2026" and "hyperscaler capex 2027" are maximally relevant to each other and must never merge. A relevance reranker therefore cannot be the identity judge on its own; it can rank, and the key decides what a high rank may mean.
